{%- comment -%}
  DRIP collection banner image.

  A full-bleed artwork band that reads straight off the collection, not off
  section settings: `custom.banner_desktop` and `custom.banner_mobile`, both
  single-image metafields. Nothing about it is authored in the customizer, so
  one section placement serves every collection that carries the metafields
  and each one shows its own artwork.

  No fixed height and no cropping. The band is exactly as tall as the supplied
  artwork is at full width, which is the only treatment that respects a
  banner someone has composed as a single flat image — an aspect-ratio box
  with `object-fit: cover` would cut type off the ends of it.

  The two images swap at 750px through <picture>, so the browser downloads one
  of them, not both. Each carries its own aspect ratio as a custom property,
  which reserves the right box before either file arrives — a full-bleed LCP
  image with no reservation is the single largest layout shift a page like
  this can have.

  Either metafield alone is enough: whichever is set is used at both
  breakpoints. With neither set the section renders nothing at all rather than
  an empty band, apart from a note in the theme editor so the gap is
  explicable.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign desktop = collection.metafields.custom.banner_desktop.value
  assign mobile = collection.metafields.custom.banner_mobile.value

  # The <img> is the mobile artwork wherever both exist, because <source> is
  # what carries the desktop one. Falling back the other way keeps a
  # desktop-only collection working.
  assign base = mobile | default: desktop
  assign wide = desktop | default: mobile

  assign banner_alt = base.alt | default: collection.title
-%}

{%- if section.settings.solid_header -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    The header is a single global instance rendered by header-group.json, so it
    cannot be styled per template from its own schema. This template opens
    directly under the bar, and the bar's usual --color-bg is the warm
    near-black ground, which reads as a smudge against artwork trimmed to true
    black. Rendered here rather than in the header's stylesheet so it applies
    wherever this section is placed and nowhere else.

    Outside the banner guard on purpose: the bar is black because of the
    template this section defines, not because a particular collection happens
    to have filled its metafields in yet.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <style>
    .drip-header {
      background-color: var(--color-bg-deep);
    }
  </style>
{%- endif -%}

{%- if base != blank -%}
  <section
    class="collection-banner-image"
    style="
      --cbi-ratio: {{ base.aspect_ratio }};
      --cbi-ratio-wide: {{ wide.aspect_ratio }};
    "
  >
    <picture>
      {%- if desktop != blank and mobile != blank -%}
        <source
          media="(min-width: 750px)"
          srcset="
            {{ wide | image_url: width: 750 }} 750w,
            {{ wide | image_url: width: 990 }} 990w,
            {{ wide | image_url: width: 1440 }} 1440w,
            {{ wide | image_url: width: 1920 }} 1920w,
            {{ wide | image_url: width: 2560 }} 2560w,
            {{ wide | image_url: width: 3200 }} 3200w
          "
          sizes="100vw"
          width="{{ wide.width }}"
          height="{{ wide.height }}"
        >
      {%- endif -%}

      {{
        base
        | image_url: width: 1600
        | image_tag:
          loading: 'eager',
          fetchpriority: 'high',
          sizes: '100vw',
          widths: '400, 600, 750, 990, 1200, 1600',
          class: 'collection-banner-image__img',
          alt: banner_alt
      }}
    </picture>
  </section>
{%- elsif request.design_mode -%}
  <section class="collection-banner-image collection-banner-image--empty">
    <p>
      Add an image to this collection&rsquo;s
      <code>custom.banner_desktop</code> or <code>custom.banner_mobile</code>
      metafield to show a banner here. Nothing renders on the live storefront
      until one of them is set.
    </p>
  </section>
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  .collection-banner-image {
    display: block;
    background-color: var(--color-bg-deep);
  }

  .collection-banner-image picture {
    display: block;
  }

  /* `height: auto` with an explicit ratio: the ratio reserves the box before
     the file lands, and auto hands the box straight back to the image once it
     has, so a ratio rounded off the metafield can never letterbox it. */
  .collection-banner-image__img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    aspect-ratio: var(--cbi-ratio, auto);
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .collection-banner-image__img {
      aspect-ratio: var(--cbi-ratio-wide, var(--cbi-ratio, auto));
    }
  }

  /* Theme editor only — see the design-mode branch above. */
  .collection-banner-image--empty {
    padding: var(--space-lg) var(--gutter);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: var(--leading-body);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .collection-banner-image--empty code {
    color: var(--brand-accent);
    font-size: inherit;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "DRIP collection banner",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "drip-collection-banner-image-section",
  "enabled_on": {
    "templates": ["collection"]
  },
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The artwork comes from the collection itself — the custom.banner_desktop and custom.banner_mobile metafields — so each collection using this template shows its own banner. There is nothing to pick here."
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "solid_header",
      "label": "Black header bar",
      "info": "Paints the header true black so it reads as one piece with a banner trimmed to black. Turn off if the banner is light.",
      "default": true
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "DRIP collection banner"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
